! The charge — a gift announces itself, the receiver ratchets

''Operator, 2026-09-13'' (quote license): on `nexus publish` — //"agree, but this whole topic needs a research spirit to collide with prior art/golden principles/anti-patterns/security concerns (new capability, needs pono design), and a clear lift into lamplighter caps (not kahu, tho many may hold both cap-sets)."//

''The lean the charge agreed with, stated as the thing this carrier tests to destruction:''

# `--apply` ''signs and announces'' on the crossroads plane, and does nothing else.
# The receiving hearth's `kāhuli grammar` — the fast ratchet — stands as ''the only door that installs''.
# `--apply` ''never ratchets''. A gift announces itself; the receiver ratchets.
# ''The lamplighter carries the basket; the kahu decides to plant.''

''What the collision did to the lean.'' It held, and the field supplied a stronger argument for it than the house had: the separation of ANNOUNCE from INSTALL reads as the ''one mitigation that survives a maintainer-key takeover'', which every other control in the stack fails (#/security). It also broke two things the house had not noticed it was missing — an offering carries ''no monotone version'' and ''no freshness lease'', so TUF's ROLLBACK and FREEZE attacks both stand open (#/security, #/questions Q1).

''And it took one warrant away.'' The clause the house leans on — //the obligation to receive is not the obligation to use// — does not appear in Mauss, who argues the other way; and the hoʻokupu reading the house likes did not resolve to a citable source. ''The lean survives on its own security argument and MUST stop borrowing the anthropology's authority'' (#/the-gift).

''What this carrier does'': it names the caps, prices the attacks, bounds `--apply`, proves the anti-roster stance against the systems that took the other road, and plans the lift red-by-red. It changes no code.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-house-today>>

!! The house today — what the founding hearth already built

!!! The door, read-only, with the offering HELD

`lares nexus publish plugins` reads the operator's own collection and builds nothing; `PUBLISHABLE = ["plugins"]` takes one case per publishable thing (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/nexus-publish.ts:29`), so a second cap arrives as a CASE rather than another door. `--apply` refuses at `:60-66` with exit 2 and states its own payload: //"mints a SIGNED offering record naming the collection, its region cid and its blob descriptors, then announces it on the crossroads plane"// (quote license). A tier named at the wrong door draws a refusal that POINTS rather than shrugs (`:94-101`).

!!! The record — one offeror, one region, one signature

`packages/lararium-mesh/src/plugin-offering.ts:36-45` carries the whole ruling in a field set: `kind` · `offeror` (//"an ed25519 verifying-key hex — a nym, never a roster seat"//, `:39`) · `pluginsCid` · `blobs` · `sig`. ''There is no slot for a co-signer.'' The mint takes the signing hand as a parameter and //"no seed reaches this module"// (`:57-65`).

!!! The verify RECOMPUTES, and that is the load-bearing move

`verifyPluginOffering` (`:76-92`) checks the signature over the offering's own bytes AND folds the blobs back through `computePluginsCid` (`:87`) — the same function the genesis bake runs (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/genesis-doc.ts:339-341`, `foldRegion("plugins/v1", …)`). Both halves fail closed. The sharp vector stands pinned: //"a SIGNED offering whose blobs fold elsewhere REFUSES — the signature never stands in for the fold"// (`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/plugin-offering.test.ts:38`).

<<~ has Built Record "at/plugin-offering.ts:36-45 carries/kind·offeror·pluginsCid·blobs·sig ~ ONE signature, no steward set (operator ruling, dcec1ef0b)">>
<<~ has Built Verify "at/plugin-offering.ts:76-92 does/signature-over-own-bytes AND blobs-fold-to-declared-region ~ fail-closed in both halves">>
<<~ has Built Antigen "at/offering-antigen.ts:129-150 does/fold VERIFIED quorum acts into the set standing aside ~ the parameter list carries NO presentations, and that absence IS the law">>
<<~ has Built Presentation "at/offering-antigen.ts:46-90 does/a tender says what it noticed ~ zero threshold weight; five honest presentations move a verdict exactly as far as none">>
<<~ has Built Domains "at/domains.ts:133,142,150 holds/plugin-offering ⊥ offering-presentation ⊥ offering-kapae ~ a signature over one can never verify as another">>

!!! The immune half stands READY, not live

`offering-antigen.ts:24-30` says so in its own header (quote license): //"Nothing calls this fold … the law here stands READY rather than enforced. A Nexus opts in by consulting it."// A self-clearing weld holds the two halves together — `offering-antigen.test.ts:132` fails the moment a production caller appears and names the cure. ''An auditor reading the offering path must not take a ready function for a live one.''

!!! ★ THE INVERSION THE HOUSE HAS NOT NOTICED ★

''The CONDEMNATION board ratchets; the OFFERING does not.'' `OfferingKapaeEntry` carries `version: number`, monotone per offering — //"a later act supersedes an earlier one; a stale entry cannot roll it back"// (`offering-antigen.ts:97-98`), pinned at `offering-antigen.test.ts:87`. `PluginOffering` carries ''no monotone field at all'' (`plugin-offering.ts:36-45`). So the house can prove a condemnation is current and ''cannot prove an offering is''. That asymmetry is the whole of #/security's freeze and rollback rows.

!!! The announce lane already exists, in another subject

`realm-bag.ts:359-379` carries the shape `--apply` wants: a `RealmBagAnnounce` under its OWN domain (`domains.ts:151`), keyed by the subject, body = //"that it exists and who keeps it. NEVER the doc"// — and `realm-plane.ts:178, 193` lands it inside a `handle.change()` on the crossroads doc. ''The offering announce asks for no new mechanism; it asks for one more subject.'' Beside it, `realm-plane.ts:173` carries the discipline `--apply` MUST borrow: //"refusing to write a registration that does not count"// — a mint self-checks before it announces.

!!! The fetch door exists too

`packages/lararium-node/src/bulb-read-face.ts:5-8` serves `/bulb/<cid>.bin` and `/cas/<cid>` GET-only, PUBLIC-floor only, //"bytes named by their own hash, no sync session"// (`:18-19`). `:99` holds the line a taker's blobs must never cross: //"a CONTRACT book rides the realm's own lane, never the shore"//.

!!! What stands UNBUILT

<<~ has Unbuilt Announce "no OFFERING_ANNOUNCE domain, no announce record, no crossroads write ~ the record exists, the publication does not">>
<<~ has Unbuilt Mint "no signing hand wired to --apply ~ nexus-publish.ts:60-66 refuses; nothing calls signPluginOffering in production">>
<<~ has Unbuilt Take "no taker's door ~ `nexus kahuli grammar --apply` itself stands HELD (nexus-kahuli.ts:73-79), and it takes no `--from`">>
<<~ has Unbuilt Caps "no `offer` · `carry` · `witness` cap names anywhere ~ vessel-caps names five caps and none of them is this">>
<<~ has Unbuilt Consult "nothing consults foldOfferingAntigen ~ offering-antigen.ts:24-30, welded at offering-antigen.test.ts:132">>

